# ML pipeline artifacts & Python tooling — large blobs / not part of the web app.
# Keep them out of the web repo so a stray `git add .` can't commit model weights.
artifacts/
artifacts_250/
artifacts_250_canonical/
# ^ the 2026-08-27 canonical+decimate ensemble. savedmodel_fold*/ below already ignores the
# weights, but not the vocab_250.json / PROVENANCE.json beside them, so the directory kept
# showing up as untracked. Ignore the whole thing, same as the two above it.
artifacts_medical/
data_medical/
# ^ the 123-class Sem-Lex clinical ensemble + its split manifest, off Kaggle 2026-09-03.
# Ignored for TWO reasons, not one:
#   1. size — 4 SavedModels + 4 EMA + 4 .weights.h5, and by_word/ is 380 MB.
#   2. LICENCE — Sem-Lex is CC BY-NC-SA. split_manifest.parquet is per-clip derived
#      metadata from a non-commercial corpus and this repo's visibility is unverified,
#      so redistributing it is Salim's judgement call, not a default.
# The files the demo needs that are SAFE to track live at the repo root instead:
# vocab_medical_123.json, word_acc_medical.json, clinical_ship_vocab.json,
# safety_gates_medical.json, topic_medical_*.json. Rebuild the rest from the Kaggle
# notebook semlex-medical-v2 -> Output -> art_medical/ + data_medical/.
semlex_metadata.csv
# ^ 91,148 rows of Sem-Lex ASL-LEX annotation. Same CC BY-NC-SA redistribution question.
gap_stats.txt
# ^ per-sequence fingerspelling metadata from the Google competition corpus. Same reason.
cand_off.csv
# ^ 6.8 MB, one row per candidate clip with its selection metrics and reject reason, keyed
# `word/participant_sequence` — per-clip GISLR metadata, so the same redistribution question
# as the two above. Nothing tracked reads it: it is the human-readable audit trail behind the
# reselect arms, and the arms themselves (clips_off/clips_2sonly.meta.json) ARE tracked
# because training/diff_reselect_arms.py defaults to them. Regenerate alongside the arms.
*_backup/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.weights.h5
*.keras
savedmodel_fold*/
web_model*/

