# Avatar deliverables from the contracted rigger (2026-09-12). Two reasons, and the second is
# the load-bearing one:
#   1. Size. `3D Char deaf.glb` is 29.2 MB, of which 28.4 MB is a single diffuse texture
#      embedded TWICE (7.8 MB WebP + 20.7 MB JPEG fallback). Geometry is 760 KB.
#   2. 🔴 LICENCE. That file is built on `rp_claudia_rigged_002` — a Renderpeople scanned
#      asset — and the rigger has not yet declared it or its licence (§16 of
#      docs/AVATAR_BRIEF_COMPLETE.md; we asked as Q5 on 2026-09-07). Renderpeople's standard
#      licence does not permit redistributing the model inside an application, which is
#      exactly what we would be doing. Committing it puts an asset we may have no right to
#      redistribute into git history PERMANENTLY, on a repo that pushes to GitHub — a rewrite
#      is the only way back out. Keep it local until the licence is answered in writing.
# The derived, licence-free artefacts under avatar/ (the bone map and the measured length
# table) ARE tracked: they are our own measurements, not his geometry.
*.glb
*.gltf
*.fbx
*.blend
*.blend1
# Anything that EMBEDS that geometry is the same asset in another wrapper, so it inherits the
# same restriction. Both are rebuilt in seconds:
#   python avatar/export_viewer_payload.py && python avatar/build_viewer.py
avatar/viewer_payload.json
avatar/sign_viewer.html

